{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And do not touch anything that is theirs, lest you be swept away</b> – The measure of the verse is: Depart now from the tents of these wicked men, lest you be swept away in all their sin, and do not touch anything that is theirs. The meaning is that if they do not depart from there, they will be swallowed up in the mouth of the earth. And he warned them not to touch in order to save any of their property and take it for themselves, for it is herem. And Rabbi Abraham said (Ibn Ezra on Numbers 16:26) that if they came to save their property, they would descend to Sheol like them, and if so, this would be like the meaning of \"and his wife looked back from behind him, and she became a pillar of salt\" (Genesis 19:26), as I mentioned in explaining his reasoning there (Ramban on Numbers 16:17)."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:06:13.110322901Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}